<title>TURKEY: Turk Ege Biracilik reports Q1 loss vs pr.</title>
<headline>Turk Ege Biracilik reports Q1 loss vs pr.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share loss   (lira)    16.71 vs	25.31 profit</p>
<p>    Loss			     35.55 vs	39.89 net profit</p>
<p>    Net sales		   1,972.70 vs   1,086.00</p>
<p>    Operating profit	     62.33 vs	66.55</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  488.32 vs     387.28</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	  92.30 vs	40.13</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 537.60 vs     241.41</p>
<p>    Extraordinary income	 50.66 vs	 2.06</p>
<p>    Total debts		 5,727.47 vs   3,239.33</p>
<p>    Equity			7,981.65 vs   4,374.75</p>
<p>    Capital		     2,128.29 vs   1,576.51</p>
<p>NOTE - Brewer Ege Biracilik ve Malt Sanayii A.S., owned largely by Turkish brewery, automotive and stationery group Anadolu Endustri Holding, plans to double its capital by issuing one bonus for one existing share from May 26.</p>
<p>It will also pay out a 200 lira cash dividend per 1,000 lira nominal valued share from 1996 profits from May 26.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
